---
title: Tuna Pasta
servings: 1
course: dinner
tags: quick, 15 minutes
image: https://img.youtube.com/vi/M-PuGg7Ek-w/maxresdefault.jpg
source: https://youtu.be/M-PuGg7Ek-w
time: 15m
---

Fill a large stainless steel #skillet{} halfway with @water and bring to a simmer. Season with @salt and add @spaghetti{100%g}, gently submerging the pasta as it softens.

Finely slice @fresh red chilli{0.5}. Crush and finely chop @garlic{1%clove}. Roughly chop @flat-leaf parsley{1%handful}.

Once the pasta is al dente, use #tongs{} to transfer it directly to a #plate{}. Ladle out and reserve about 60 ml of the starchy @water{60%ml} in a cup, then discard the rest of the cooking water.

Return the skillet to the heat and add @extra virgin olive oil{2%tbsp}. Add the garlic and chilli, sauteing for ~{30%seconds} until fragrant, and season with a pinch of @salt.

Drain most of the oil from @canned tuna in olive oil{1%can} and add the tuna chunks to the skillet, keeping them intact.

Return the pasta to the pan along with @caper{1%tbsp} and the reserved starchy @&water. Toss and stir vigorously over medium-high heat until the water and oil emulsify into a glossy sauce.

Remove from the heat. Finely grate the zest of @lemon{1} over the pasta and squeeze in about 15 ml of lemon juice. Toss through the chopped parsley and transfer to a plate to serve.
